From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: EddizEge <300900304+EddizEge@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 05:55:38 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] freedreno/common: Full sysmem depth CCU cache on Adreno 840
 (guess)

GUESS, NOT CONFIRMED: no Adreno 840 has run with this change yet.

On three Adreno 840 phones Ocarina of Time loses the device at the first
render pass over its 12288x12288 D16 (UBWC) depth target; the Adreno 830
runs it. The only render-backend cache setting that differs between the
two is the sysmem depth CCU cache: the 840 takes a8xx_gen2's
THREE_QUARTER fraction with 192KB per CCU, the 830 a8xx_gen1's FULL
with 256KB.

Mesa MR 46016 (airidosas252, open draft) found that THREE_QUARTER
deadlocks sysmem passes that write UBWC depth on the X2-90, another
a8xx_gen2 GPU, and moves that GPU to FULL/256KB. This is the same change
for both A840 entries (3 slice 0xffff44050A31, 2 slice 0xffff44050A21),
re-done by hand against db6c407 (the MR's own commit touches only the
X2-90 entry). The 840's GMEM mode already uses a FULL 256KB depth cache,
and only the sysmem RB_CCU_CACHE_CNTL depth size and offset change: the
depth cache moves down by num_ccu * 64KB from the top of GMEM. GMEM
tiling, the 830 and every other GPU are unchanged.

Runtime equivalent without this patch:
FD_DEV_FEATURES=sysmem_ccu_depth_cache_fraction=0:sysmem_per_ccu_depth_cache_size=262144

Idea from: https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/mesa/mesa/-/merge_requests/46016
Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/freedreno/common/freedreno_devices.py | 12 ++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/freedreno/common/freedreno_devices.py b/src/freedreno/common/freedreno_devices.py
index 63abb5ccfbb..dc87e858d5b 100644
--- a/src/freedreno/common/freedreno_devices.py
+++ b/src/freedreno/common/freedreno_devices.py
@@ -1563,7 +1563,12 @@ add_gpus([
     ], A6xxGPUInfo(
         CHIP.A8XX,
         [a7xx_base, a7xx_gen3, a8xx_base, a8xx_gen2,
-         GPUProps(shading_rate_matches_vk = True)],
+         GPUProps(shading_rate_matches_vk = True,
+                  # Anka Turnip guess: the a8xx_gen2 THREE_QUARTER sysmem depth
+                  # cache may deadlock sysmem passes that write UBWC depth (Mesa
+                  # MR 46016 on X2-90). Use a830's full 256KB per CCU instead.
+                  sysmem_ccu_depth_cache_fraction = CCUColorCacheFraction.FULL.value,
+                  sysmem_per_ccu_depth_cache_size = 256 * 1024)],
         num_ccu = 6,
         num_slices = 3,
         tile_align_w = 96,
@@ -1583,7 +1588,10 @@ add_gpus([
     ], A6xxGPUInfo(
         CHIP.A8XX,
         [a7xx_base, a7xx_gen3, a8xx_base, a8xx_gen2,
-         GPUProps(shading_rate_matches_vk = True)],
+         GPUProps(shading_rate_matches_vk = True,
+                  # Same guess as the 3 slice a840 above.
+                  sysmem_ccu_depth_cache_fraction = CCUColorCacheFraction.FULL.value,
+                  sysmem_per_ccu_depth_cache_size = 256 * 1024)],
         num_ccu = 4,
         num_slices = 2,
         tile_align_w = 64,
